window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Joshua Macallan knew the space shuttle would explode.</b><i> </i>That is why he was in Florida in January of 1986. He was trying to save the crew and <i>finally make a difference</i> after so many failures. Like when he tried to save Kennedy in ’63. Joshua was naive and full of hope.</p> <p><i>That was then.</i> Now he is an old man with a past composed of more tragedy than triumph. The FBI watches Joshua’s every move. Even though he currently lives in a Kansas nursing home staring at a blank wall most of the day. When he is not rambling about Victoria, that is. The young woman who had visited him on the farm in 1958 claiming to be from the future. She had done a lot of talking. He had fallen in love. Then <b>Victoria disappeared.</b></p> <p>Until now.</p> <p>Riots are brewing in New York City over a controversial new technology. He sees Victoria on the news. <i>Still alive</i> and still as young as his memories of her. He needs answers. Joshua will head for the chaos in New York with his 5-year-old granddaughter in tow. Sure, the FBI will be after him. And his son. But finally, after all these years, <b>Joshua Macallan has hope again.</b></p>"; 
